{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"witted-invisible-roan","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observed\nOn 2026-09-02 the configured rebar MCP endpoint initially accepted tracker calls and started plan-review job 1788399093580353346-ab9badfce4eb4b45a6db70794296455e. A later status poll returned \"Transport closed\"; every subsequent rebar MCP call returned nginx HTTP 502 for more than 20 minutes, including a fresh user-requested retry. The local CLI remained functional.\n\n## Impact\nAgents cannot poll gate results, claim work, or perform tracker operations through the required MCP surface. Long gate state is ambiguous and restarting it risks duplicate billed work.\n\n## Reproduction\n1. Start an async plan review through MCP.\n2. Poll gate_status for its job handle.\n3. Observe transport closure followed by persistent HTTP 502 responses.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- The deployed MCP endpoint remains reachable during and after long async gate jobs.\n- An unhealthy upstream is detected and recovered or reported with an actionable health signal.\n- A regression test or operational probe covers loss of the MCP upstream while a gate job is active.","id":"9ea3-7d07-ea55-4496","parent_id":"","priority":1,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["bug","mcp","availability","ops"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Configured rebar MCP endpoint returns persistent HTTP 502 after async gate start"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788411304995986001,"uuid":"97efd87a-2d6b-4333-a55e-5833d9d07cce"}